{
  "account": "plur",
  "background": { "color": "#0A0A0A" },
  "slides": [
    {
      "type": "cover",
      "main": [
        "RENEGADE",
        "HARDWARE"
      ],
      "sub": "The underground lab that built the darkest machines."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "1995. Southwest London.",
        "Two people wanted a label",
        "that would stand by the underdog.",
        "Clayton Hines and Mark Hill.",
        "They didn't want to build something popular.",
        "They wanted to build something true."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Their first release:",
        "Future Forces — Flash Gordon.",
        "The duo behind it: Darren White and Jason Maldini.",
        "You might know Darren White by another name.",
        "dBridge.",
        "Bad Company UK."
      ],
      "sub": "It started here."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "1995.",
        "DJ Trace took T Power's Mutant Jazz",
        "and broke it open.",
        "A sound with no name started to form.",
        "Clinical. Dark. Machine-heavy.",
        "Trace and Ed Rush called it: Techstep."
      ],
      "sub": "That word was born here."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "19 July 1997.",
        "Renegade Hardware took their first night",
        "to The End, London.",
        "They stayed for 11 and a half years.",
        "No other drum and bass night ran longer there."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Trace. Dom & Roland. Konflict.",
        "Technical Itch. Loxy. Ink. Raiden.",
        "They didn't chase radio play.",
        "They chased depth.",
        "Over 100 releases.",
        "Zero compromise."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "quote",
      "quote": [
        "Konflict. Messiah. 2002.",
        "Two producers.",
        "One of the heaviest DnB tracks ever made.",
        "Renegade Hardware didn't explain itself.",
        "It just hit you."
      ],
      "note": "The sound that needed no words."
    },
    {
      "type": "cta",
      "text": [
        "6 February 2016. The Final Chapter.",
        "The Coronet, London.",
        "80 DJs. 20 MCs. 10 hours. 5 rooms.",
        "20 years of the underground,",
        "done properly."
      ],
      "strobe": "20 years",
      "cta": "Save this."
    }
  ]
}
